- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): The source explicitly assigns the process to the "Part Provision Team", but the model assigns all nodes to a "Default" actor, violating SMC7.
- action(n1, "start"): The source description does not document a "start" task or step; this node hallucinates behavior not present in the text, violating SMC1.
- action(n11, "End"): The source states "the process comes to an end", describing a process termination boundary rather than an executable task. Declaring it as an `action` misrepresents its semantic role, violating SMC2.
- precedence(b2, c2) & guard(b2, c2, ...): The source states that if parts are supplied, the team "can also continue with the process". The model routes this branch directly to the convergence node `c2`, omitting the explicitly documented "continue with the process" step, violating SMC1.